    "result": "Excellent! All tests are passing and all public exports are preserved. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. **Fixed governance exports** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\nAdded named exports for the schema constants that were being imported from `schema.js`. The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` directly from `index.js` but it wasn't being re-exported.\n\n**What was fixed:**\n- Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n- This fixed the test: \"flags schema violations with descriptive errors\"\n\n### 2. **Fixed toxicity metric evaluation** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\nThe `toxicityMetric` function was receiving references as a second parameter (which was being interpreted as banned terms), causing incorrect toxicity scores. Created a wrapper function that only passes the outputs.\n\n**What was fixed:**\n- Created `toxicityMetricWrapper` that only passes outputs to `toxicityMetric`\n- Updated `DEFAULT_METRICS` to use the wrapper instead of the raw function\n- This fixed the test: \"runs default evaluations\" (toxicity score now correctly returns 1 for clean outputs)\n\n**All 28 tests now pass** \u2713",
